﴿And for them therein are benefits﴾, from their hides, their wool, and other things;

﴿and drinks﴾, from the milk. It is the plural of "mashrab" (مَشْرَب), which means the place of drinking, or "al-shirb" (الشِّرْب) [meaning the drinking itself];

﴿Will they not then be grateful?﴾ to God for the bounty of the livestock?!
